["document.info", {"title": "Parabolic solar cooker", "description": "A parabolic solar cooker whose dish is made of flat petals (gores) cut from aluminium, polypropylene or cardboard sheet and covered with reflective foil, riveted to a rim hoop. Each petal's outline is drawn from the paraboloid's arc length; bent, the petals approximate the dish z = r^2 / 4f. The dish turns on an axis through the focus in a fork on a turning base, so the pot stays level at the focus. Set the diameter, the focal ratio, the number of petals, the sheet, the pot and the sun's elevation. Export the sets Cut sheet: petals and Steel parts with File > Export... (DXF or SVG). Never look into the focus, never leave it without a pot: it gets very hot.", "author": "3DCraft Jigs", "licence": "CC-BY-4.0", "url": "https://github.com/johancoppens/3dcraft-jigs/tree/main/jigs/solar-cooker", "tags": ["solar cooker", "parabolic dish", "gores", "cut sheet", "laser cutting", "formula"]}],
